This essay presents a formal mathematical interpretation of Juyoung Kim‚Äôs framework </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Emotion as Rhythmic Inference}, a theory positing that consciousness emerges from rhythmic imperfection‚Äîan interplay among uncertainty, informational gaps, and resonance. We extend the framework by developing explicit equations for the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Gap Consciousness Theory}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Phase Alignment Theory}, and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Curvature of Affect}, situating them within information geometry and active inference. Consciousness is modeled as a dynamic trajectory on a curved manifold of beliefs, with emotion functioning as curvature in this manifold. Resonance corresponds to phase‚Äêsynchronized inference between systems. The result is a unified mathematical structure linking affective dynamics, learning, and relational artificial intelligence.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{abstract}

