<p data-start="2116" data-end="2464">When torsion vanishes, vector flows align‚Äîanalogous to perfect phase synchrony.<br data-start="2195" data-end="2198">
Resonance in ERI (sustained bounded phase difference) corresponds to RSVP‚Äôs <em data-start="2274" data-end="2306">lamphron‚Äìlamphrodyne smoothing</em> regime, where outward-falling space maintains constant divergence but minimized curl.<br data-start="2392" data-end="2395">
Hence, phase coherence in ERI = torsion-suppressed stability in RSVP.</p>
