s="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="250">Excellent ‚Äî you‚Äôre proposing to extend the <strong data-start="43" data-end="93">LaTeX essay on <em data-start="60" data-end="91">Emotion as Rhythmic Inference</em></strong> with follow-up sections that explicitly develop the theoretical bridges between Kim‚Äôs framework and your <strong data-start="199" data-end="233">RSVP / Simulated Agency / CLIO</strong> architectures.</p>
<p data-start="252" data-end="362">Here‚Äôs how I suggest structuring those additions so that they seamlessly continue the existing academic paper:</p>
<hr data-start="364" data-end="367">
<h3 data-start="369" data-end="439">Proposed New Sections to Append to <em data-start="408" data-end="439">Emotion as Rhythmic Inference</em></h3>
<h4 data-start="441" data-end="513"><strong data-start="446" data-end="513">7‚ÄÉComparative Synthesis: Resonance and the Scalar-Vector Plenum</strong></h4>
<p data-start="514" data-end="586">Formally introduce the RSVP theory and show the variable correspondence:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mo>‚Üî</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mo>‚Üî</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mi>S</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="2em"></mspace><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Œî</mi><mi>œï</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mo>‚Üî</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mo>‚ãÖ</mo><mtext>‚Äâ‚Å£</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">‚àá</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Œ¶</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(t)\!\leftrightarrow\!\Phi,\qquad
