</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>*{Appendix A: Field Equations and Simulation Schema}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.1‚ÄÉRhythmic Scalar‚ÄìVector Field Equations}
The unified Lagrangian introduced in Section 13 yields, via
Euler‚ÄìLagrange variation with respect to the scalar field~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
vector field~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and entropy field~</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
the following dynamical system:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{align}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}
     +</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dot</span></span><span> S
     +</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\eta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mu</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>R, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>[4pt]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})
     +</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>)
     -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nu</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>[4pt]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> S}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>= D</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2 S
     +</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{v})
     +</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>f(U)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>G</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>R(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>),
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{align}
where:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}[leftmargin=1.2em]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nu</span></span><span>,D</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>S,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are coupling
      constants controlling the rates of entropic advection,
      diffusion, and resonance feedback;
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Tr}(R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{ij})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the Ricci scalar of the affective
      curvature;
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f(U)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>G</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are the local uncertainty and gap functions
      defined in Section 2.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}
The first equation governs scalar potential oscillations,
the second describes vector-torsion dynamics,
and the third expresses entropic growth driven by resonance.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.2‚ÄÉDimensionless Formulation}
For numerical convenience we rescale variables as
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>'=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>/</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
