</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.6‚ÄÉInterpretation}
In steady state, the system self-organizes into quasi-periodic
patterns where scalar, vector, and entropic fields oscillate with
slight phase offsets.
Regions of high resonance exhibit low torsion and high curvature,
mirroring emotional coherence.
When the resonance amplitude exceeds a threshold, a new attractor
emerges‚Äîinterpreted phenomenologically as a
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{moment of insight or consciousness}.
The lattice model therefore operationalizes both Kim‚Äôs rhythmic
inference and the RSVP entropic plenum within a single computational
experiment.

