The author gratefully acknowledges the interdisciplinary
conversations and writings that inspired this synthesis.
Conceptual guidance was drawn from the convergent traditions of
neuroscience, physics, and phenomenology, particularly the works that
explore consciousness as a non-equilibrium and information‚Äìgeometric
phenomenon.
Special recognition is due to the communities investigating the
Free Energy Principle and Active Inference,
whose formal rigor provided the mathematical substrate for much of the
analysis, and to ongoing philosophical dialogues on
affective resonance and embodied cognition,
which have illuminated the phenomenological dimensions of these models.

The synthesis also benefited from exchanges among researchers working
at the intersection of thermodynamics, semiotics, and cognitive
architecture.
Their efforts to bridge symbolic and energetic formulations
have advanced the broader project of understanding consciousness as
a rhythmic, self-organizing field.
Any remaining speculative or interpretive extensions are, of course,
the author‚Äôs own responsibility.

