<h3 data-start="3417" data-end="3435">Notes on usage</h3>
<ul data-start="3436" data-end="3961">
<li data-start="3436" data-end="3580">
<p data-start="3438" data-end="3580">The bibliography reflects both <strong data-start="3469" data-end="3482">empirical</strong> and <strong data-start="3487" data-end="3502">theoretical</strong> sources relevant to <em data-start="3523" data-end="3554">Emotion as Rhythmic Inference</em> and the RSVP synthesis.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3581" data-end="3700">
<p data-start="3583" data-end="3700">The Kim (2025) citation is formatted as a <strong data-start="3625" data-end="3644">conference talk</strong>, consistent with the YouTube transcript you supplied.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3701" data-end="3827">
<p data-start="3703" data-end="3827">The Barandes (2024) and Friston et al. references bridge your framework to contemporary quantum and active-inference work.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3828" data-end="3961">
<p data-start="3830" data-end="3961">All citations compile cleanly with <code data-start="3865" data-end="3909">\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{References}</code> already included for table of contents consistency.</p>
</li>
</ul>
