"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="208">Excellent ‚Äî I can produce a <strong data-start="28" data-end="71">fully citation-integrated LaTeX version</strong> of your essay so that every theoretical claim, comparison, and equation is properly supported with the citations from the BibTeX file.</p>
<p data-start="210" data-end="444">Before I do that, I just need to confirm two quick formatting preferences so the inline citation style matches your target venue or archive (for example, <em data-start="364" data-end="399">Frontiers in Systems Neuroscience</em>, <em data-start="401" data-end="410">Entropy</em>, or arXiv philosophy of science):</p>
<ol data-start="446" data-end="899">
<li data-start="446" data-end="660">
<p data-start="449" data-end="480"><strong data-start="449" data-end="478">Citation style preference</strong></p>
<ul data-start="484" data-end="660">
<li data-start="484" data-end="550">
<p data-start="486" data-end="550">(A) Author‚Äìyear format <em data-start="509" data-end="550">(e.g., ‚Äúas proposed by Friston (2010)‚Äù)</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="554" data-end="660">
<p data-start="556" data-end="660">(B) Parenthetical format <em data-start="581" data-end="608">(e.g., ‚Äú(Friston, 2010)‚Äù)</em><br data-start="608" data-end="611">
‚Üí Which would you prefer for the compiled PDF?</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="662" data-end="899">
<p data-start="665" data-end="689"><strong data-start="665" data-end="687">Bibliography style</strong></p>
<ul data-start="693" data-end="899">
<li data-start="693" data-end="770">
<p data-start="695" data-end="770">(A) <code data-start="699" data-end="708">apalike</code> (default humanities/social sciences look, open parentheses)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="774" data-end="845">
<p data-start="776" data-end="845">(B) <code data-start="780" data-end="790">plainnat</code> (technical sciences look, compact numerics optional)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="849" data-end="899">
<p data-start="851" data-end="899">(C) <code data-start="855" data-end="865">unsrtnat</code> (numerical order of appearance)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="901" data-end="1154">Once you confirm those, I‚Äôll insert the actual <code data-start="948" data-end="958">\citep{}</code> and <code data-start="963" data-end="972">\cite{}</code> commands in the correct places throughout your essay (Parts I‚ÄìV, Future Research, and General Synthesis) and return the complete LaTeX text ready to compile with your <code data-start="1140" data-end="1146">.bib</code> file.</p>
