</span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Emotion as Rhythmic Inference: Toward a Unified Framework for Affective Resonance**</span></span><span>  
</span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">_A comparative and mathematical synthesis between Juyoung Kim‚Äôs theory of rhythmic inference and the Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum (RSVP) field framework._</span></span><span>

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## Abstract</span></span><span>

This paper formalizes Juyoung Kim‚Äôs ‚ÄúEmotion as Rhythmic Inference‚Äù as a dynamic field-theoretic model of affective resonance and compares it with the RSVP (Œ¶, v, S) framework for non-equilibrium consciousness. It integrates Kim‚Äôs triadic principles‚ÄîGap Consciousness, Phase Alignment, and Resonance‚Äîwith RSVP‚Äôs scalar, vector, and entropic dynamics to produce a unified mathematical description of consciousness as rhythmic disequilibrium. The synthesis introduces formal equations for phase alignment, curvature of affect, and resonance Hamiltonians, developing an explicit thermodynamic and information-geometric bridge between phenomenology and field theory.

