</span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Author:**</span></span><span> Flyxion Research Group  
</span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Date:**</span></span><span> \today  
</span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Repository:**</span></span><span> https://github.com/standardgalactic/rhythmic-inference  

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## Abstract</span></span><span>

This paper develops a unified theoretical and mathematical synthesis between  
Juyoung Kim‚Äôs </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*Emotion as Rhythmic Inference*</span></span><span> and the </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*Relativistic Scalar‚ÄìVector Plenum (RSVP)*</span></span><span> field theory.  
It formalizes emotion and consciousness as coupled non-equilibrium processes of rhythmic inference,  
where meaning emerges through dynamic phase alignment, informational curvature, and resonance.  
The framework integrates phenomenological insights from affective neuroscience with field-theoretic formulations of  
non-equilibrium thermodynamics and active inference.  
Consciousness, in this model, is not the product of equilibrium but of sustained rhythmic tension ‚Äî  
the managed imperfection that fuels growth, adaptation, and relational understanding.

