</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Comparative Diagnostics of Rhythmic Theories}

The framework of Rhythmic Inference can be evaluated through the lens of the
diagnostic criteria proposed in the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Typology of Theoretical Failure},
which assesses the structural rigor of scientific theories
in terms of dimensional, energetic, and informational coherence.
When examined under these criteria, the rhythmic model satisfies
the core conditions of theoretical viability.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Dimensional Coherence}

Kim‚Äôs core variables‚Äîgap (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>), phase (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>), and resonance (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>)‚Äî
are dimensionless yet derivable from measurable observables
such as amplitude, coherence, and phase lag.
They preserve unit consistency across levels of description,
addressing the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{dimensional drift} problem
identified as a hallmark of theoretical collapse in
unconstrained cognitive models </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\citep</span></span><span>{typology2025failure}.
Each term can be traced to an empirical domain:
gap to prediction-error magnitude,
phase to oscillatory timing,
and resonance to bounded energy exchange.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Injectivity and Surjectivity}

The rhythmic mapping between internal inference and external rhythm
maintains injectivity:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\det</span></span><span>(J</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\top</span></span><span>}J) &gt; 0,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
ensuring that distinct predictive states correspond to distinct
affective trajectories.
This property prevents the degeneracy typical of syntactic mimicry
in non-embodied AI systems.
Surjectivity is likewise maintained insofar as all observable affective
phenomena can be expressed within the rhythmic manifold,
avoiding the under-representation that marks empirically unfalsifiable
frameworks.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Energetic Feasibility}

The phase-gradient term </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{2}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
corresponds to affective tension or the work of emotional regulation.
Minimizing this quantity yields the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Work of Understanding}
functional:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
W = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\int</span></span><span> |</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{2}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> dV,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
which parallels the epistemic-energy term described in the typology.
Emotional regulation thus acquires a concrete thermodynamic meaning:
to sustain coherence, a system must dissipate finite energy
in proportion to its predictive curvature.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropy Balance}

Resonant inference also satisfies the entropic bound
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
W </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\geq</span></span><span> k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{B}T</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> S,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
implying that meaning formation carries a minimal energetic cost.
This condition guarantees thermodynamic sustainability:
affective resonance cannot exceed the system‚Äôs
available free energy without collapse into incoherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Mapping Rhythmic Inference onto the Epistemic Energy Functional}

The </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Epistemic Energy Functional} introduced in the typology
provides a quantitative lens for evaluating theoretical stability:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
R[f,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>]
  = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\det</span></span><span>(J</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\top</span></span><span>}J)
  - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span>|</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{2}
  - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> S.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Here </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes the mapping from environmental stimuli
to internal affective states,
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> the phase difference between prediction and sensation,
and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> the change in affective uncertainty.
Under Rhythmic Inference,
consciousness maintains </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> through periodic error correction,
occupying the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{reflective-rigour regime}
where informational curvature and energetic cost remain balanced.

