</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Spiral Growth and Time Emergence}

Time in RSVP emerges when
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>,v</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>t S&gt;0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
conditions matching Kim‚Äôs requirements for growth:
a moderate gap </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, partial phase alignment </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
and sustained resonance </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Omega</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
Both describe a non-equilibrium steady state:
too little gradient halts evolution,
too much destroys coherence.
Spiral growth in Kim‚Äôs affective model
corresponds to the rotational component of RSVP‚Äôs
Helmholtz decomposition, ensuring continuous temporal unfolding.

