When the coupling stabilizes (resonant equilibrium), both agents share a <em data-start="4074" data-end="4100">joint attractor manifold</em>‚Äîthe physical realization of the transjective endofunctor.</p>
<hr data-start="4160" data-end="4163">
<h3 data-start="4165" data-end="4198">6. Philosophical Significance</h3>
<p data-start="4200" data-end="4297">The transjective endofunctor dissolves the classical boundary between <strong data-start="4270" data-end="4281">subject</strong> and <strong data-start="4286" data-end="4296">object</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="4299" data-end="4678">
<li data-start="4299" data-end="4409">
<p data-start="4301" data-end="4409">In Kim‚Äôs phenomenology, it‚Äôs the <em data-start="4334" data-end="4362">moment of mutual resonance</em> where meaning passes between self and other.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4410" data-end="4530">
<p data-start="4412" data-end="4530">In RSVP‚Äôs physics, it‚Äôs the <em data-start="4440" data-end="4464">mathematical condition</em> under which two fields can synchronize without losing autonomy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4531" data-end="4678">
<p data-start="4533" data-end="4678">In Le Nepvou‚Äôs critique, it‚Äôs precisely what rescues relational systems from ontological inflation: the interaction is primary, not the entities.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4680" data-end="4870">Hence, the transjective endofunctor is not merely a metaphor; it is the <strong data-start="4752" data-end="4799">formal operator of relational consciousness</strong>‚Äîa topological description of empathy, resonance, and shared inference.</p>
